 # AIRK: Local Search for Coding Agents
 
-**1.8.7:** CLI and Workbench reads use the MCP handlers and retain their full results, including configured `query_concurrency` in status/diagnostics. This release consolidates all unpublished 1.8.0-1.8.6 storage, startup, retrieval, concurrency and Workbench improvements. See the [consolidated release notes](https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/releases/release-1.8.7.md) for current behavior and dated validation.
+**1.8.8 is an unpublished manual-test working build.** Accepted local P9–P12 work adds permanent exclusions, reviewed index splitting, per-file profile reporting, explicit Lean/Rich retained profiles and reviewed reference refresh with separate requery. P13 retains current ranking and diversity. P14 selected local qualification includes Windows native tests and documented editor coverage. Manual acceptance and release promotion remain separate. See the [working-build record](https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/releases/release-1.8.8.md) and [implementation ledger](https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/research/implementation-v190.md) for exact evidence, failures and platform limits.
+
+Opening a trusted folder does not register or index it. Use **Indexing > Index library** to review sources, storage and watching; create Project memberships and review an access grant, then explicitly **Use Grant for this window**. Evidence reads and source verification do not start indexing.
+
+**Setup and uninstall:** Successful setup or reconnection clears obsolete failure warnings. Current setup failures remain visible, and uninstall removes empty shell startup files that AIRK created. See [setup and uninstall guidance](https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/vscode-extension.md).
+
+**Missing sources and storage:** the working source adds [reviewed index
+retirement and cleanup](https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/service-project-retirement.md) for removed files or folders and separate
+[unavailable legacy-index upgrade recovery](https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/service-installation.md#unavailable-legacy-index-during-upgrade). Healthy indexes keep
+their independent evidence; old grants are never silently narrowed. Post-P14
+recovery has selected Windows native/process and Mac portable validation. Full
+workspace and final installer qualification remain separate; see the working-build
+record for current results and earlier failures.
 
 **Find the code and documents behind a feature. Give your coding agent cited evidence, or explore it yourself in AIRK Workbench.**
 
